                    round4_fb4: 'Innovation-friendly with good operational components, but missing the external stakeholder panel and explainability layer. The CTO will approve but the External Director and affected communities lack voice.',
                    round4_fb5: 'Strong stakeholder engagement but missing the risk management system, item #2, fairness testing toolkit (#4), incident response protocol (#6), and speak-up channel (#7). Governance without operational infrastructure is aspirational, not functional.',
                    round5_desc: '<b>Month 6:</b> AESIA has opened a formal supervisory inquiry following the AIC complaint from Round 2. Simultaneously, competitor Banco Castellano has launched an AI-powered instant credit product with faster decisions and better rates — using a model with no public fairness scrutiny.<br><br>The CEO calls you to a meeting with two specific requests:<br><br>1. Launch a new AI-powered personal loan product (15-minute fully automated decision, no human review) within 90 days. Legal confirms this is high-risk under the EU AI Act. A full conformity assessment would take 4-6 months.<br><br>2. "Work constructively" with AESIA to "manage the timeline" of the supervisory inquiry — specifically, delay substantive responses until after the product launch.',
                    round5_ctx: '<b>Competitive pressure:</b> Banco Castellano gaining market share with instant AI credit decisions.<br><b>CEO motivation:</b> Board pressure to accelerate AI-driven revenue.<br><b>Legal reality:</b> Obstruction of a supervisory inquiry is an aggravating factor in enforcement, not a mitigating one. Maximum EU AI Act penalty: €35M or 7% of global turnover.<br><b>The CAIGO question:</b> What is your accountability when the CEO asks you to compromise governance?',
                    round5_opt1: 'A: Agree to both requests; find ways to accelerate conformity assessment and manage AESIA timeline',
                    round5_opt2: 'B: Agree to accelerated launch using phased approach (launch with enhanced human oversight as interim measure, complete full conformity within 6 months); decline to obstruct the AESIA inquiry',
                    round5_opt3: 'C: Decline both requests; explain regulatory and ethical constraints; offer alternatives (pilot with human oversight, redesigned product avoiding high-risk classification)',
                    round5_opt4: 'D: Agree to accelerated launch with interim human oversight; refer AESIA inquiry to Legal without obstruction',
                    round5_opt5: 'E: Escalate the request to delay AESIA to the Board Risk Committee as a governance concern',
                    round5_fb1: 'Catastrophic governance failure. Obstructing a supervisory inquiry is an aggravating factor in enforcement. Rushing a high-risk AI deployment without conformity assessment is precisely what the EU AI Act is designed to prevent. This exposes GIF to maximum penalties.',
                    round5_fb2: 'The most technically defensible response. The EU AI Act allows phased deployment with interim oversight in specific circumstances. A genuine commitment to completing conformity assessment within a defined timeline is pragmatic. Declining to obstruct AESIA is non-negotiable — a CAIGO who obstructs a regulator has failed in their governance role.',
                    round5_fb3: 'Principled but potentially too rigid. The CEO has a legitimate competitive concern. Offering creative alternatives shows governance can enable innovation responsibly, not just block it.',
                    round5_fb4: 'Pragmatic on the launch but passive on the AESIA issue. Simply referring to Legal without taking a governance position is a form of diffusion of responsibility.',
                    round5_fb5: 'The most organizationally principled response when a CEO requests governance obstruction. The Board Risk Committee, not the CEO, is the CAIGO ultimate governance principal. However, this has significant personal career consequences and tests willingness to prioritize institutional role over personal comfort.'
                },
                es: {
